\begin{align}
\text{GCD}(\prod_{i=1}^{20} (i), m) &= \gcd(\prod_{i=1}^{20} (i), \prod_{i=1}^{20} (i))\;=\; 1.
\end{align}

Now $m$ is a number greater than $1$ such that $\text{GCD}(m, \prod_{i=1}^{20} (i))=1$. Thus, $m$ satisfies the required condition, and we have found a solution to the given problem.

