\end{align*}

A mistake was made; the given equation has extraneous solutions caused by the multi-valued function $\arccos$. Let's add the solutions from the other two quadrants, that is, from $\pi + \frac{\pi}{3}$ to $2\pi + \frac{\pi}{3}$ and $4\pi + \frac{\pi}{3}$ to $5\pi + \frac{\pi}{3}$:

\begin{align*}
\theta_1 &= \frac{\pi}{3} + 2\pi\\
